Interestingly, Amelia's ending her show.

102
00:08:58.960 --> 00:09:06.200
Very interestingly and very notably, but of course, holding on to the IP and leveraging that IP into something potentially bigger and broader.

103
00:09:06.440 --> 00:09:12.840
And she's working on a movie, and she I think she has bigger aspirations, at least for her profile.

104
00:09:12.840 --> 00:09:18.840
I don't know if she'll ever be able to match the economics of what that show delivers, but maybe she will.

105
00:09:18.840 --> 00:09:19.480
Right.

106
00:09:19.480 --> 00:09:25.080
But I think so, we have brand deals, if you like, as the as the lowest hanging fruit on the tree.

107
00:09:25.080 --> 00:09:35.480
And I think what we've seen, particularly with um CAA, where of course I was an agent and they've done a brilliant job, I think, of building out not just their creator division, but their brands group.

108
00:09:35.480 --> 00:09:48.040
And so when it comes to supporting their creator clients with securing bigger and more expansive, more interesting brand partnerships, that's of course you know, a traditional aspect of this.

109
00:09:48.040 --> 00:10:03.240
